wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">fresh mint leaves</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">aromatic and cooling</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoons</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">olive oil</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for a healthy fat</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">lemon juice</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">adds a zing of freshness</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">clove</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">garlic, minced</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">adds a kick of flavor</span></li></ul></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Seasoning</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">to taste</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\"> </span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Salt and pepper</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for seasoning</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-3488-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"3488\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 large bowl&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For mixing the greens and dressing.</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Small bowl&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For whisking the dressing.</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Knife&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For chopping the greens.</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 whisk&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For mixing the dressing.</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-3488-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-3488-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"3488\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Preparation Steps</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3488-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Start by washing your spinach and kale thoroughly. Once clean, chop them into bite-sized pieces. This will make them easier to enjoy!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3488-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Next, take your fresh mint leaves and tear them into smaller, bite-sized pieces. This releases their lovely aroma and flavor!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3488-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">In a small bowl, whisk together olive oil, lemon juice, minced garlic, salt, and pepper. This dressing will bring everything together beautifully!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3488-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">In a large bowl, combine the chopped greens and torn mint. Give them a gentle toss to mix them up a bit.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3488-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Drizzle your delicious dressing over the greens and toss everything together until well coated. Serve immediately for maximum freshness and enjoy your minted greens!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-3488-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrient</th>\n<th>Amount per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>150</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>10g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>3g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>15g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to whip up some refreshing minted greens!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Fresh-Ingredients-for-Minted-Greens.webp\" alt=\"Fresh ingredients for minted greens on a wooden kitchen table, including spinach, kale, mint, olive oil, lemon, garlic, and seasoning.\" class=\"wp-image-3486\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Fresh-Ingredients-for-Minted-Greens.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Fresh-Ingredients-for-Minted-Greens-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>2 cups fresh spinach</strong> – fresh and vibrant leaves</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 cups kale</strong> – massaged or chopped for tenderness</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/2 cup fresh mint leaves</strong> – aromatic and cooling</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 tablespoons olive oil</strong> – for a healthy fat</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 tablespoon lemon juice</strong> – adds a zing of freshness</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 garlic clove, minced</strong> – adds a kick of flavor</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Salt and pepper to taste</strong> – for seasoning</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-minted-greens\"><strong>How to Make Minted Greens</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to whip up a fresh and vibrant dish! This recipe takes about 10 minutes to prepare, with no cooking time required. Just a little time for the flavors to mingle, and you’re all set!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Step-by-Step-Preparation-of-Minted-Greens.webp\" alt=\"A step-by-step visual guide to preparing minted greens, featuring fresh ingredients and preparation methods.\" class=\"wp-image-3487\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Step-by-Step-Preparation-of-Minted-Greens.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Step-by-Step-Preparation-of-Minted-Greens-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Wash and Chop</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Start by washing your <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spinach\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">spinach</a> and kale thoroughly. Once clean, chop them into bite-sized pieces. This will make them easier to enjoy!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Tear the Mint</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Next, take your fresh mint leaves and tear them into smaller, bite-sized pieces. This releases their lovely aroma and flavor!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Make the Dressing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a small bowl, whisk together olive oil, lemon juice, minced <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garlic\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">garlic</a>, salt, and pepper. This dressing will bring everything together beautifully!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Combine the Greens</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a large bowl, combine the chopped greens and torn mint. Give them a gentle toss to mix them up a bit.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Dress and Serve</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Drizzle your delicious dressing over the greens and toss everything together until well coated. Serve immediately for maximum freshness and enjoy your minted greens!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Salad</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>Mediterranean</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>0 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>0 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Vegetarian</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Fresh and immediately after preparation!</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-minted-greens\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making Minted Greens</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Choose fresh, vibrant greens for the best flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Chop mint finely to release its essential oils.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Mix in a splash of lemon juice for a zesty kick.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with a drizzle of olive oil for richness.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve immediately to enjoy the freshness.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-minted-greens\"><strong>How to Serve this minted greens</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Top your favorite grilled chicken or tofu with minted greens for a fresh twist.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Mix minted greens into a vibrant salad with cherry tomatoes and cucumbers.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve as a zesty side with roasted vegetables or quinoa.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Incorporate into a wrap with hummus and fresh veggies for a quick lunch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Blend into a refreshing smoothie with spinach and a splash of lemon juice.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Storing and enjoying your minted greens later is easy!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Cool the minted greens to room temperature.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Transfer to an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Place cooled minted greens in freezer-safe bags.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Remove excess air before sealing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and freeze for up to 2 months.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw frozen minted greens in the refrigerator overnight.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Reheat in a skillet over medium heat for best texture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add a splash of vegetable broth to keep them moist.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. What greens go with mint?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Mint pairs beautifully with a variety of greens, including spinach, arugula, and kale. These greens not only complement the refreshing flavor of mint but also add a vibrant color and texture to your dishes. You can toss them together in salads, blend them into smoothies, or use them as a base for grain bowls to create a delightful and nutritious meal.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. How do you do minted peas?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>To make minted peas, start by cooking fresh or frozen peas in boiling water until tender, about 2-3 minutes. Drain and return them to the pot. Add a generous handful of fresh mint leaves, a squeeze of lemon juice, and a pinch of salt. Stir gently to combine, allowing the heat to release the mint&#8217;s aroma. This simple dish is a perfect side for any meal, adding a burst of flavor and freshness.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. How to cook seasonal greens?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Cooking seasonal greens is easy and rewarding! Start by washing the greens thoroughly to remove any dirt. You can sauté them in a bit of olive oil with garlic for added flavor, or steam them lightly to retain their nutrients. Season with salt, pepper, and a splash of lemon juice to enhance their natural taste. Seasonal greens like Swiss chard, collard greens, or mustard greens can be enjoyed as a side dish or incorporated into soups and stews.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. What goes with mint peas?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Minted peas pair wonderfully with a variety of dishes. They complement grilled chicken, fish, or lamb beautifully. You can also serve them alongside roasted vegetables or mix them into a grain salad for added texture and flavor. For a vegetarian option, try them with quinoa or couscous, and don’t forget to sprinkle some feta cheese on top for a delicious twist!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">So there you have it—minted greens are not just a dish, but a delightful experience waiting to happen! Whether you toss them in a salad or use them as a vibrant garnish, these greens are sure to bring a smile to your face. Enjoy the simplicity and the burst of flavor they add to your meals. Happy cooking!</p>\n",
